D3D12: a texture barrier side with AccessBits::NONE and a defined layout gets SYNC_NONE.

CommandBufferD3D12::Barrier converts a texture barrier side by side: GetBarrierSyncFlags derives
SyncBefore / SyncAfter from the stages alone, GetBarrierAccessFlags maps AccessBits::NONE to
D3D12_BARRIER_ACCESS_NO_ACCESS, and the layout comes from g_BarrierLayouts (since enhanced barriers
came in, 1d52b40). The debug layer refuses a texture barrier whose side has NO_ACCESS, a layout
other than UNDEFINED and a sync other than SYNC_NONE (1331, INCOMPATIBLE_BARRIER_VALUES), and the
enhanced-barriers spec gives SYNC_NONE / NO_ACCESS as the form for a side that only transitions the
layout. On Vulkan the same NRI barrier is an execution dependency on the stages with an empty access
mask, which is legal (it chains after a semaphore wait), so a portable caller writes it; D3D12 then
records an invalid barrier and Close fails.

This sets SyncBefore / SyncAfter to SYNC_NONE for a side whose access is NONE and whose layout is not
UNDEFINED. Buffer and global barriers have no layout and are unchanged; a side with access or with
an UNDEFINED layout is unchanged. Measured on v190 with Agility 1.619, NVIDIA, NRI validation off, a
4x4 RGBA8 texture: {NONE, COPY_DESTINATION, COPY} -> {SHADER_RESOURCE, SHADER_RESOURCE, ALL_SHADERS}
gave "[1331] ID3D12CommandList::Barrier: Invalid LayoutBefore value D3D12_BARRIER_LAYOUT_COPY_DEST.
LayoutBefore must be LAYOUT_UNDEFINED or SyncBefore must be SYNC_NONE when AccessBefore is
ACCESS_NO_ACCESS in texture barrier at group [0], index [0]." and Close E_INVALIDARG (likewise for
LayoutAfter, and for GENERAL / SHADER_RESOURCE on both sides); with the change all record clean.

diff --git a/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
index c69bd54..777edb1 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/CommandBufferD3D12.hpp
@@ -2443,6 +2443,13 @@ NRI_INLINE void CommandBufferD3D12::Barrier(const BarrierDesc& barrierDesc) {
                 out = {};
                 out.SyncBefore = GetBarrierSyncFlags(in.before.stages, in.before.access);
                 out.SyncAfter = GetBarrierSyncFlags(in.after.stages, in.after.access);
+
+                // "NO_ACCESS" with a defined layout requires "SYNC_NONE" (D3D12 debug layer, 1331): the layout transition is the only thing this side does
+                if (in.before.access == AccessBits::NONE && in.before.layout != Layout::UNDEFINED)
+                    out.SyncBefore = D3D12_BARRIER_SYNC_NONE;
+                if (in.after.access == AccessBits::NONE && in.after.layout != Layout::UNDEFINED)
+                    out.SyncAfter = D3D12_BARRIER_SYNC_NONE;
+
                 out.AccessBefore = GetBarrierAccessFlags(in.before.access);
                 out.AccessAfter = GetBarrierAccessFlags(in.after.access);
                 out.LayoutBefore = GetBarrierLayout(in.before.layout, in.before.access);
